1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:04,311
The Tormentor: a puppeteer who prefers you to do the dying yourself, in her traps.

2
00:00:04,531 --> 00:00:05,832
Here's how she plays.

3
00:00:06,667 --> 00:00:08,744
The Tormentor doesn't start on the board.

4
00:00:08,744 --> 00:00:12,341
Keep the Setup card face up, and keep the other Setup cards nearby too.

5
00:00:12,561 --> 00:00:16,767
Shuffle the seven Victim Death Trap cards into one deck and the four Final Girl

6
00:00:16,767 --> 00:00:18,364
Death Trap cards into another.

7
00:00:18,584 --> 00:00:22,458
Put a Victim on the space where the Killer would start, and immediately put it in a

8
00:00:22,458 --> 00:00:23,299
Victim Death Trap.

9
00:00:24,133 --> 00:00:28,046
Until the Finale is revealed, ignore the Killer Actions on Terror cards:

10
00:00:28,046 --> 00:00:29,296
no moving or attacking.

11
00:00:29,516 --> 00:00:33,687
If an effect places something or counts spaces from the Killer, reveal a random

12
00:00:33,687 --> 00:00:36,749
Setup card and use its Killer space, then shuffle it back.

13
00:00:36,749 --> 00:00:38,967
If it says to place the Killer, ignore it.

14
00:00:39,187 --> 00:00:43,431
Once the Finale is revealed, she appears at the start of the next Killer phase, on

15
00:00:43,431 --> 00:00:47,623
the Killer space of a random Setup card, and resolves the Finale's Killer Actions

16
00:00:47,623 --> 00:00:48,296
from then on.

17
00:00:49,100 --> 00:00:52,215
The two Death Trap icons set a trap on a Victim, or on you.

18
00:00:52,435 --> 00:00:56,459
Draw a card from the matching deck, put its Death Trap token in the target's space,

19
00:00:56,459 --> 00:00:59,465
and move the target's meeple onto the START space of the card.

20
00:00:59,465 --> 00:01:00,435
They're now Trapped.

21
00:01:00,655 --> 00:01:04,004
The Tormentor never targets Trapped people unless a card says so.

22
00:01:04,833 --> 00:01:08,774
Trapped people can't move and ignore all movement effects, including panic.

23
00:01:08,774 --> 00:01:12,663
The one exception: you can use movement towards completing an Escape Task.

24
00:01:12,883 --> 00:01:16,211
While you're Trapped you can't play Reaction cards, search, or attack Enemies.

25
00:01:16,431 --> 00:01:20,566
If it's unclear whether a Trapped person counts as being on the board, use the Game

26
00:01:20,566 --> 00:01:23,855
Ambiguity rules, and if still unsure, treat them as off the board.

27
00:01:24,667 --> 00:01:29,114
When you see the progress icon, move every trapped meeple one space along its card

28
00:01:29,114 --> 00:01:33,507
and apply the effect it lands on. For example, three trapped Victims landing on a

29
00:01:33,507 --> 00:01:36,164
Horror icon, a Horror icon, and a two-Time space:

30
00:01:36,164 --> 00:01:38,171
raise Horror twice and lose two Time.

31
00:01:38,391 --> 00:01:41,541
When a Victim reaches the final space, the trap is complete.

32
00:01:41,541 --> 00:01:45,217
They're killed, Bloodlust rises, and you apply the card's Fail Result.

33
00:01:45,437 --> 00:01:49,380
If your own meeple reaches the end of a Final Girl trap, you're killed and lose

34
00:01:49,380 --> 00:01:51,925
straight away, without revealing your Final Health.

35
00:01:51,925 --> 00:01:56,117
Losing your health normally before then still flips your Final Health token, and you

36
00:01:56,117 --> 00:01:56,765
stay trapped.

37
00:01:56,985 --> 00:02:01,205
Victims in a space with a completed trap panic in the Panic phase, and completed

38
00:02:01,205 --> 00:02:02,681
traps are removed in Upkeep.

39
00:02:03,500 --> 00:02:07,696
Each trap lists Escape Tasks. While on its space, or trapped in it yourself, you can

40
00:02:07,696 --> 00:02:11,543
work on them, in order from top to bottom, marking each one off as it's done.

41
00:02:11,763 --> 00:02:15,383
Swinging Blades, for example: first, time the blades, five Time.

42
00:02:15,383 --> 00:02:18,495
Then cut the ropes, two damage. Lastly, dive to safety:

43
00:02:18,495 --> 00:02:19,400
move two spaces.

44
00:02:19,620 --> 00:02:21,912
When the last task is done, the person is free:

45
00:02:21,912 --> 00:02:25,423
put their meeple on the trap's space and remove the trap token and card.

46
00:02:26,233 --> 00:02:30,073
Spending Time on a task is only allowed if it wouldn't take your Time below zero.

47
00:02:30,293 --> 00:02:33,447
Any effect counts towards a task while you're in the space.

48
00:02:33,447 --> 00:02:37,457
But using a card for a task replaces its normal effect, and excess is lost.

49
00:02:37,457 --> 00:02:41,947
A double-success Sprint can complete Move one space, but the extra moves vanish, and

50
00:02:41,947 --> 00:02:44,032
you still lose the Time the card costs.

51
00:02:44,252 --> 00:02:48,184
You can use several cards on one task, but you must finish it before the Action

52
00:02:48,184 --> 00:02:52,216
phase ends or the progress is lost. If you're trapped yourself, you can't work on

53
00:02:52,216 --> 00:02:53,660
Victims' traps in your space.

54
00:02:53,880 --> 00:02:58,332
And if at least one untrapped Victim is with you, add one die to Horror rolls for

55
00:02:58,332 --> 00:03:02,179
Action cards used on Escape Tasks. Just one die, however many Victims.

56
00:03:03,000 --> 00:03:07,115
When a Terror card shows this icon, put it face down on the bottom of the Terror

57
00:03:07,115 --> 00:03:11,128
deck. If it's the only card left, or cards keep looping, discard them instead.

58
00:03:11,933 --> 00:03:16,059
Overkill Traps: when a Victim is killed by a Death Trap, you and every Victim in

59
00:03:16,059 --> 00:03:17,245
that space take damage.

60
00:03:17,465 --> 00:03:21,898
The Epic Endless Traps: each time a Victim is freed, put a new Victim Death Trap on

61
00:03:21,898 --> 00:03:25,103
the farthest Victim. If there's no Victim to trap, you lose.

62
00:03:25,323 --> 00:03:29,322
Let's Play a Game traps a Victim, choosing by the first condition that fits:

63
00:03:29,322 --> 00:03:33,637
in the farthest exit space from you, on any exit space, next to an exit, or simply

64
00:03:33,637 --> 00:03:34,795
the farthest from you.

65
00:03:35,600 --> 00:03:38,273
No Escape!: she heads for the closest unlocked exit.

66
00:03:38,273 --> 00:03:41,254
When she ends her move on one, place a Locked token there.

67
00:03:41,254 --> 00:03:45,469
No Victim can be saved at a locked exit. If every exit is locked at the start of a

68
00:03:45,469 --> 00:03:49,787
Killer phase, you lose. If you can unlock one, she has to go back and lock it again.

69
00:03:50,007 --> 00:03:53,015
Game Over: she moves and attacks, then moves and attacks again.

70
00:03:53,235 --> 00:03:56,795
The Ultimate Trap puts you in a Death Trap, and she can attack you while you're in

71
00:03:56,795 --> 00:03:56,925
it.

72
00:03:57,733 --> 00:04:01,770
A few tips. You can't save everyone: give up on traps that are too far away and take

73
00:04:01,770 --> 00:04:02,299
the Horror.

74
00:04:02,519 --> 00:04:05,996
Bring an untrapped Victim with you for the extra die on Escape Task rolls.

75
00:04:06,216 --> 00:04:09,735
If you're ever trapped, escape first: it's an instant loss otherwise.

76
00:04:09,735 --> 00:04:13,151
Players win about seventy-two per cent of logged games against her.

77
00:04:13,151 --> 00:04:13,661
Good luck.

